flyExplorer
===========

flyExplorer is a Windows file manager. The canonical product on main is the
C++/WinRT WinUI 3 application under app/winui.

Quick start (Windows)
---------------------

For normal use, build once with "fly.bat build" and then double-click
run.bat in the repository root, or double-click the built
out\winui\Release\flyExplorer.exe directly. No PowerShell is needed.
run.bat never rebuilds automatically; when launched by double-click with
no arguments it keeps a missing-build error visible.

For development, use the single entry point:

    fly.bat help
    fly.bat check
    fly.bat build
    fly.bat run
    fly.bat run "D:\My Files"
    fly.bat test gui
    fly.bat test policy
    fly.bat package

"fly.bat package" intentionally clears out\, performs a fresh Release build,
regenerates and verifies the exact-runtime provenance, then builds the
unsigned installer. It stops on the first failure; it also updates tracked
packaging/licenses/PAYLOAD_PROVENANCE.* metadata. Do not invoke this expensive
workflow as a default compile/test step.

Older build.bat, run.bat, test.bat, clean.bat and package.bat commands are
kept for compatibility. Internal app/winui and tests/winui build.cmd scripts
remain implementation details. The "full" test stage runs Release build +
functional GUI by default, not a complete native/Debug/visual acceptance.

Canonical layout
----------------

    app/winui/        WinUI 3 product, XAML, helper and project templates
    src/base/         UI-independent native core
    tests/winui/      source contracts, owned GUI tests and native fixtures
    tools/winui/      canonical local orchestration
    docs/development/ maintained current engineering documentation
    out/              ignored build products/intermediates
    .cache/nuget/     ignored NuGet cache
    logs/             ignored local evidence

Release output is out\winui\Release\flyExplorer.exe. Do not copy the EXE
alone; sibling WinUI resources and FlyShellIsolationHelper.exe are required.

The retired MFC product is recoverable only from Git revision cbffb48.
Historical migration reports and legacy HTML Help are no longer kept in the
working tree; Git history is their recovery source.

See docs/development/CURRENT_STATUS.md for revision-scoped acceptance evidence
and open release gates. Since 2026-10-10, flyExplorer no longer owns a
self-hosted Windows Runner, control/remote-shell branch or Windows Actions
workflows. Normal main pushes do not trigger Windows acceptance.

Use tngkrwlsmd/personal-control-plane for Windows operations. Its Remote Shell
accepts requests targeting windows-vm; manual central-flyexplorer-ci.yml
acceptance uses project_id=desktop-a, an exact 40-character commit_sha reachable
from flyExplorer/main, and an explicit scope (health, source, release, gui or
gui-probe). Health and gui-probe are not product acceptance; gui proves
functional GUI, not visual pixels or the former Debug+Release full suite.
Check active jobs and the request lease before dispatch. The current contract
is in docs/operations/windows-runner-retirement.md and root AGENTS.md.

For flyExplorer, root AGENTS.md overrides the vendored generic branch-first
Git example: prefer verified logical units directly on main when safe and
permitted, using short-lived work branches only when required. Preserve
evidence/remote-windows as a historical evidence archive.

